  "question": {
    "text": "If $z=\\sin \\theta-i \\cos \\theta,$ then for any integer $n$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$z^{n}+\\frac{1}{z^{n}}=2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{n \\pi}{2}-n \\theta\\right)$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$z^{n}+\\frac{1}{z^{n}}=2 \\sin \\left(\\frac{n \\pi}{2}-n \\theta\\right)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$z^{n}-\\frac{1}{z^{n}}=2 i \\sin \\left(n \\theta-\\frac{n \\pi}{2}\\right)$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$z^{n}-\\frac{1}{z^{n}}=2 i \\cos \\left(\\frac{n \\pi}{2}-n \\theta\\right)$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A",
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $z=\\sin \\theta-i \\cos \\theta$\r\n$=\\cos \\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)+i \\sin \\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=e^{i(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{2}).}$\r\nNow. $z^{n}=e^{i(n\\theta-\\frac{n\\pi}{2}).}=\\cos \\left(n \\theta-\\frac{n \\pi}{2}\\right)+i \\sin \\left(n \\theta-\\frac{n \\pi}{2}\\right)$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{z^{n}}=e^{i\\left(\\frac{n \\pi}{2}-n\\theta\\right)}=\\cos \\left(n \\theta-\\frac{n \\pi}{2}\\right)-i \\sin \\left(n \\theta-\\frac{n \\pi}{2}\\right)$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad z^{n}+\\frac{1}{z^{n}}=2 \\cos \\left(n \\theta-\\frac{n \\pi}{2}\\right)=2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{n \\pi}{2}-n \\theta\\right)$\r\nand $z^{n}-\\frac{1}{z^{n}}=2 i \\sin \\left(n \\theta-\\frac{n \\pi}{2}\\right)$"
  }
}